272
00:15:03,780 --> 00:15:06,440
He was Ushiwaka's right-hand man in that old story.

273
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:07,040
Hey, Rayon!

274
00:15:07,160 --> 00:15:07,660
What's up?

275
00:15:08,020 --> 00:15:08,500
Rayon?

276
00:15:09,100 --> 00:15:11,800
That little Karasuno score just called you Benkei.

277
00:15:11,860 --> 00:15:13,420
Where the heck did he get that name from?

278
00:15:13,900 --> 00:15:14,500
I don't know.

279
00:15:14,680 --> 00:15:15,480
I don't really get it.

280
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:19,160
That shorty is half of Karasuno's quick attack duo.

281
00:15:19,520 --> 00:15:19,820
What?

282
00:15:20,060 --> 00:15:20,520
For real?

283
00:15:21,460 --> 00:15:22,480
Let's do this!

284
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:24,820
Aw, look at that little tweet down there.

285
00:15:24,900 --> 00:15:26,020
He's so small.

286
00:15:26,680 --> 00:15:28,200
What if he's subbing for someone?

287
00:15:28,700 --> 00:15:29,720
He's kind of cute.

288
00:15:30,020 --> 00:15:32,140
I have a thing for rooting for the underdog.

289
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:34,460
Not a kill!

290
00:15:35,260 --> 00:15:36,080
All right, you two.

291
00:15:36,260 --> 00:15:37,340
Do what you did yesterday.

292
00:15:37,340 --> 00:15:42,140
One last thing, and I can say this with great confidence.

293
00:15:42,820 --> 00:15:45,840
You are every bit as good at this game as they are.

294
00:15:46,800 --> 00:15:51,460
Just remember, take control from the start.

295
00:15:55,460 --> 00:15:59,380
What just happened?

296
00:15:59,540 --> 00:16:00,660
He shot it straight down?

297
00:16:00,980 --> 00:16:02,100
He's a quick one!

298
00:16:02,420 --> 00:16:04,040
Did the center even touch the ball?

299
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:07,620
You know, guys, I was bummed that Seizhou didn't come this year.

300
00:16:07,880 --> 00:16:09,660
But they seem pretty fun, too.

301
00:16:09,980 --> 00:16:10,880
You got that right.

302
00:16:11,300 --> 00:16:14,200
Whatever they throw at us, we will be sure to force them to surrender!

303
00:16:14,940 --> 00:16:17,300
You shouldn't talk smack if you can't back it up.

304
00:16:18,100 --> 00:16:19,600
Nah, nah, play nice.

305
00:16:19,780 --> 00:16:21,100
Don't you worry about it, Goshki.

306
00:16:21,140 --> 00:16:22,760
Your words are as cool as your bangs.

307
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:24,200
Oh, yeah? You think so?

308
00:16:24,560 --> 00:16:27,480
You know, I don't think it's a good idea to baby him the way you do.

309
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:28,740
Easy, man.

310
00:16:29,020 --> 00:16:30,520
You're too tight, Taichi.

311
00:16:30,780 --> 00:16:32,420
I have faith in this fella.

312
00:16:32,420 --> 00:16:34,240
This guy's the chosen one.

313
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:36,980
He's gonna be the ace after us third years are gone, you know?

314
00:16:38,780 --> 00:16:40,360
I won't let you down!

315
00:16:41,620 --> 00:16:42,680
Yeah, we know.

316
00:16:42,880 --> 00:16:44,920
Just do your best, Mr. Future Ace.

317
00:16:45,100 --> 00:16:47,080
Stop. You're gonna make his ego even worse.

318
00:16:47,700 --> 00:16:49,200
Okay, we're first to receive.

319
00:16:49,680 --> 00:16:50,720
Roger that, buddy.

320
00:16:51,180 --> 00:16:52,320
Kick some ass for us.

321
00:16:52,680 --> 00:16:54,500
You have to pull your own weight, too.

322
00:16:54,820 --> 00:16:56,400
Don't just lean on Ushiwaka.

323
00:16:56,900 --> 00:16:59,400
Sorry to put too much pressure on him, Ben-K.

324
00:16:59,700 --> 00:17:00,100
Ushiwaka!

325
00:17:00,100 --> 00:17:07,100
In this next game, I promise I'm going to prove myself worthy of the title of Future Ace of Shira Torizawa.

326
00:17:11,100 --> 00:17:12,880
Oh, yeah? Do your best, then.

327
00:17:12,880 --> 00:17:18,300
I think he's actually being sincere, even if he sounds like a deadpan jerk.

328
00:17:20,860 --> 00:17:23,160
Their starting lineup is just what we thought.

329
00:17:23,540 --> 00:17:24,700
Did everybody study up?

330
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:25,620
Yeah!

331
00:17:26,180 --> 00:17:28,480
Everyone needs to keep a level head out there.

332
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:31,300
If these guys take a point, get it back.

333
00:17:31,940 --> 00:17:35,200
Ushiwaka is only human, and he's bound to slip up.

334
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:37,400
You know what to do, right?

335
00:17:37,520 --> 00:17:37,880
Right!

336
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:42,260
Remember, you guys, this is the finals.

337
00:17:42,640 --> 00:17:45,900
We've made it this far, so let's win and make our way to nationals!

338
00:17:45,900 --> 00:17:58,020
We will now begin the final game of the National High School Volleyball Qualifying Tournament.

339
00:17:58,740 --> 00:18:03,560
This game determines Miyagi's representative and the overall winner of all boys' teams.

340
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:08,980
Our challengers are Karasano High School and Shira Torizawa Academy.

341
00:18:09,700 --> 00:18:11,920
Please give them a warm welcome.

342
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:14,820
This is it?

343
00:18:16,100 --> 00:18:19,480
Wow, the show looks really tiny down there, doesn't he?

344
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:22,480
Jeez, are we sure they aren't playing against college kids?

345
00:18:22,480 --> 00:18:29,360
Whoa, they've got cameras everywhere in here.

346
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:35,060
At this time, I'd like to introduce Karasano High School's starting lineup.

347
00:18:35,980 --> 00:18:38,560
Number one, Daichi Sawamura.

348
00:18:42,560 --> 00:18:46,340
Number three, Asahi Adumane.

349
00:18:49,340 --> 00:18:52,460
Number five, Ruinosuke Adumane.

350
00:18:52,480 --> 00:18:53,140
Asahi Adumane.

351
00:18:56,080 --> 00:18:59,160
Number nine, Togeo Kageyama.

352
00:19:01,460 --> 00:19:04,920
Number ten, Shouyo Hinata.

353
00:19:08,560 --> 00:19:11,660
Eleven, Kei Tsukishima.

354
00:19:11,940 --> 00:19:13,560
Suki, look who's here!

355
00:19:14,040 --> 00:19:14,860
Keep it doing!

356
00:19:14,860 --> 00:19:16,740
Number four, Libero.

357
00:19:17,200 --> 00:19:18,320
Yu Nishinoya.

358
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:20,380
Oh yeah!

359
00:19:20,380 --> 00:19:24,940
And their coach, Itetsu Takeda.

360
00:19:26,460 --> 00:19:33,460
And now, please allow me to introduce the players of Shira Torizawa Academy's starting lineup.

361
00:19:34,600 --> 00:19:37,580
Number one, Wakatoshi Ushijima.

362
00:19:40,480 --> 00:19:43,720
Number four, Weyuan Ohira.

363
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:48,940
Number five, Sasaya Tendo.

364
00:19:48,940 --> 00:19:52,540
Number eight, Stomu Goshiki.

365
00:19:53,580 --> 00:19:56,720
Number ten, Kinjiru Shirabu.

366
00:19:58,920 --> 00:20:02,140
Number twelve, Taichi Kawanishi.

367
00:20:03,260 --> 00:20:07,120
Number fourteen, Libero Hayato Yamagata.

368
00:20:08,900 --> 00:20:11,600
And their coach, Tanji Washijo.

369
00:20:13,180 --> 00:20:18,300
Ladies and gentlemen, please give the athletes of both teams a round of applause.

370
00:20:18,940 --> 00:20:21,040
Our game will begin momentarily.

371
00:20:22,540 --> 00:20:24,740
Man, you can get the Jinjin in here with a knife.

372
00:20:24,980 --> 00:20:27,080
Our guys look like they're ready and raring to go, though.

373
00:20:27,360 --> 00:20:29,580
They've got their game faces on, especially Hinata.

374
00:20:30,540 --> 00:20:32,940
Shira Torizawa's done all this a million times already.

375
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:35,380
But it's our guys' first time in center court.

376
00:20:35,820 --> 00:20:37,100
First time in the finals, too.

377
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:40,580
So you know our guys will be nervous, but you can't blame them.

378
00:20:41,380 --> 00:20:44,620
It's their first final, which means they've never played a five-set match before.

379
00:20:44,760 --> 00:20:45,540
Five sets?

380
00:20:45,780 --> 00:20:46,400
That's right.

381
00:20:46,520 --> 00:20:49,120
Up until today, they've always played best two out of three.

382
00:20:49,260 --> 00:20:51,800
But during the finals, it'll be best three out of five.

383
00:20:51,800 --> 00:20:54,260
It's just like the professional matches on TV.

384
00:20:54,660 --> 00:20:55,020
Wow.

385
00:20:55,260 --> 00:20:56,360
They're gonna be exhausted.

386
00:20:57,200 --> 00:20:57,680
Probably.

387
00:20:59,280 --> 00:21:00,480
Stamina's a big concern.

388
00:21:02,520 --> 00:21:04,820
Well, I think the best baby won't fix it!

389
00:21:09,500 --> 00:21:11,580
This looks like a different start than usual.

390
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:12,980
Yeah, you're right.

391
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:15,580
They normally kick off a game with Hinata up front and center.

392
00:21:15,580 --> 00:21:19,560
I guess they're trying to put the tall guys in front to deal with Ushiwaka.

393
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:23,660
I'm curious to see how they handle his spikes.

394
00:21:26,800 --> 00:21:27,640
Bring it!

395
00:21:31,500 --> 00:21:35,560
But I don't have time for a team that couldn't beat Alba Josai in the prelims.

396
00:21:35,720 --> 00:21:37,680
You can talk all you want, but I'm not listening.

397
00:21:41,320 --> 00:21:42,340
Serve it up, Captain!

398
00:21:45,580 --> 00:21:57,620
I got it!

399
00:21:59,280 --> 00:21:59,880
Ushiwaka!

400
00:22:03,300 --> 00:22:04,320
Here it comes.

401
00:22:11,920 --> 00:22:12,880
It's mine!

402
00:22:15,580 --> 00:22:22,700
Nice kill!

403
00:22:22,920 --> 00:22:24,360
Ushiwaka!

404
00:22:25,500 --> 00:22:26,440
Ushiwaka!

405
00:22:27,400 --> 00:22:28,320
Ushiwaka!

406
00:22:28,600 --> 00:22:29,320
Good try!

407
00:22:29,700 --> 00:22:31,420
Get the next one!

408
00:22:39,820 --> 00:22:41,820
Oh, I see, Lefty.

409
00:22:41,820 --> 00:22:45,260
Who needs help?

410
00:23:01,340 --> 00:23:04,720
Ushiwaka!

411
00:23:04,720 --> 00:23:34,700
Thank you.

412
00:23:35,700 --> 00:23:40,780
ここに高く生きたいのだ

413
00:23:40,780 --> 00:23:44,160
あとは君次第です

414
00:23:44,160 --> 00:23:48,460
全部君次第

415
00:23:48,460 --> 00:23:52,480
きっと甘い甘いと言われても

416
00:23:52,480 --> 00:23:55,080
違うよ 違う 溶けなされたって

417
00:23:55,080 --> 00:23:57,800
あとは君次第

418
00:23:57,800 --> 00:23:59,860
迷うんじゃない

419
00:23:59,860 --> 00:24:04,840
君次第

420
00:24:04,840 --> 00:24:34,820
ご視聴ありがとうございました

